---
description: NestJS backend engineering rules
globs: ["services/api/**/*.ts", "services/api/**/prisma/**", "services/api/**/package.json"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/ENGINEERING_STANDARDS.md`.

Rules:
- NestJS + TypeScript + PostgreSQL + Prisma.
- Controllers handle transport concerns; domain/business logic belongs in appropriate services/modules.
- Validate inputs at trust boundaries.
- Keep payment-provider APIs behind a provider adapter.
- Design webhook handlers for authenticated, idempotent processing.
- Persist auditable ledgers for money-adjacent rewards and inventory movement.
- Do not silently swallow errors.
- Avoid generic repositories/services unless they solve a real repeated problem.
- Business state transitions must be explicit and testable.
